Notebook[{Cell["Partonic Born cross sections: every massless 2 -> 2 QCD \
channel in D dimensions", "Title"], Cell["The lowest-order hard cross \
sections of all massless two-parton scattering channels with a tagged \
(observed) final-state parton, in D = 4 - 2 eps dimensions, for the spin \
average (UU) and for the double-longitudinal helicity difference of the \
incoming partons (LL).  They are used as the Born terms and as the \
lower-order ingredients of the collinear counterterms of the NLO \
proton-proton classes (Processes/Hadronic), and as the resolved-photon Born \
terms of the lepton-proton cross sections.  (The transverse spin transfers \
needed for the Collins effect are computed in \
Processes/Collins.)\n\nKinematics: a(pa) + b(pb) -> c(p) + d(pd), s = \
(pa+pb)^2, t = (pa-p)^2, u = (pb-p)^2, s + t + u = 0.  Output: \
Results/Born.wl with, for every channel \"a b -> c\", the squared matrix \
element averaged over the spins and colours of a and b and summed over those \
of c and d, divided by gs^4, as a function of s, t, D, CF, CA (TF = 1/2 is \
FeynCalc's normalization; u = -s-t).  The hard cross section s E dsigma/d^3p \
of the tagged parton is |M|^2/(16 Pi^2 s v) delta(1-w) with v = 1 + t/s \
(docs/CONVENTIONS.md).\n\nFlavours: q is a quark of flavour i, qp a quark of \
a different flavour k, qb and qpb their antiquarks, g the gluon; FeynArts' \
SMQCD model represents q and qp by the up quark (generation 1) and the charm \
quark (generation 2); the photon, weak bosons, leptons and down-type quarks \
are excluded.  Identical particles: when the tagged parton has an identical \
unobserved partner (q q -> q q) the identical-particle factor 1/2 is \
cancelled by the two ways of tagging, so no factor is applied; this is the \
convention of the reference codes.\n\nSpin densities (HVBM scheme; all four \
external momenta are four-dimensional): UU averages with 1/2 per incoming \
quark and 1/(D-2) per incoming gluon; LL inserts p-slash gamma5/2 for an \
incoming quark (-p-slash gamma5/2 for an incoming antiquark, whose \
positive-helicity spinor sum is (1 - gamma5) p-slash/2) and the circular \
density i eps^{mu nu l r}/(2 l.r) for an incoming gluon l (helicity + minus \
helicity -, including the factor 1/2; r is the other incoming momentum), so \
that the LL result is (sigma(++) - sigma(+-))/2 for the helicities of a and \
b, the other spins summed.  $LeviCivitaSign = -1 (Tr[gamma^a gamma^b gamma^c \
gamma^d gamma5] = -4 i eps^{abcd}), as in the lepton processes.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Load", "Section"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["LoadFeynCalc[]", "Input"], Cell["Channels and diagrams", "Section"], 
  Cell["The particle names map to FeynArts fields; a channel is {a, b, c} \
with the tagged parton c, the unobserved parton d follows from flavour \
conservation.  All channels needed by the collinear counterterms of the 16 \
proton-proton classes and by the resolved-photon terms are included; \
incoming-leg permutations are separate channels because t is defined with the \
first incoming parton.", "Text"], Cell["field = <|\"q\" -> F[3, {1}], \"qb\" \
-> -F[3, {1}], \"qp\" -> F[3, {2}], \"qpb\" -> -F[3, {2}], \"g\" -> \
V[5]|>;\nexcluded = {S[_], U[_], V[1 | 2 | 3], F[1 | 2 | 4], F[3, \
{3}]};\nchannels = {\n  {\"q\", \"qp\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qp\", \"qp\"}, \
{\"qp\", \"q\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qpb\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qpb\", \"qpb\"}, \
{\"qpb\", \"q\", \"q\"},\n  {\"q\", \"q\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"q\"}, \
{\"q\", \"qb\", \"qb\"}, {\"qb\", \"q\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"qp\"}, \
{\"q\", \"qb\", \"qpb\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"g\"},\n  {\"q\", \"g\", \"q\"}, \
{\"g\", \"q\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"g\", \"g\"}, {\"g\", \"q\", \"g\"}, {\"qb\", \
\"g\", \"qb\"}, {\"g\", \"qb\", \"qb\"}, {\"qb\", \"g\", \"g\"},\n  {\"g\", \
\"g\", \"g\"}, {\"g\", \"g\", \"q\"}, {\"g\", \"g\", \"qb\"},\n  {\"qb\", \
\"qpb\", \"qb\"}, {\"qb\", \"qp\", \"qb\"}, {\"qb\", \"qb\", \"qb\"}, \
{\"qb\", \"q\", \"qb\"}, {\"qb\", \"q\", \"g\"}, {\"qb\", \"q\", \
\"qp\"}};\nname[{a_, b_, c_}] := a <> \" \" <> b <> \" -> \" <> \
c;\nflavourNumber[x_] := Switch[x, \"q\", {1, 0}, \"qb\", {-1, 0}, \"qp\", \
{0, 1}, \"qpb\", {0, -1}, \"g\", {0, 0}];\npartner[{a_, b_, c_}] := \
Module[{ok = Select[Keys[field], Total[flavourNumber /@ {a, b}] === \
Total[flavourNumber /@ {c, #}] &]},\n  Require[Length[ok] == 1, \"The \
unobserved parton of \" <> name[{a, b, c}] <> \" is not unique\", ok]; \
First[ok]];\ndiagrams = Association @ Table[name[ch] -> \
InsertFields[CreateTopologies[0, 2 -> 2],\n  {field[ch[[1]]], field[ch[[2]]]} \
-> {field[ch[[3]]], field[partner[ch]]},\n  InsertionLevel -> {Classes}, \
Model -> \"SMQCD\", ExcludeParticles -> excluded], {ch, \
channels}];\nMap[Length, diagrams]", "Input"], Cell["Paint[diagrams[\"q g -> \
q\"], ColumnsXRows -> {3, 1}, Numbering -> Simple, SheetHeader -> None, \
ImageSize -> {600, 200}]", "Input"], Cell["Squared matrix elements", 
   "Section"], Cell["FCFAConvert gives the amplitude of each channel; \
FeynCalc forms the square: the quark spinors are closed by FermionSpinSum \
(with the densities of the spin case inserted for the incoming quarks), \
external gluons are summed with the physical polarization sum -g^{mu nu} + \
(l^mu r^nu + r^mu l^nu)/(l.r) with a reference vector r (another external \
momentum; gauge invariance makes the result independent of it), or with the \
circular density for a polarized incoming gluon; the colour sums are done by \
SUNSimplify.", "Text"], Cell["FCClearScalarProducts[];\nSetMandelstam[s, t, \
u, pa, pb, -p, -pd, 0, 0, 0, 0];\nScan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {pa, pb, \
p, pd}];\nFCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"];\n$LeviCivitaSign = \
-1;\namplitude[ch_] := Total[FCFAConvert[CreateFeynAmp[diagrams[name[ch]], \
Truncated -> False, PreFactor -> 1],\n  IncomingMomenta -> {pa, pb}, \
OutgoingMomenta -> {p, pd}, UndoChiralSplittings -> True, ChangeDimension -> \
D,\n  List -> True, SMP -> False, Contract -> False, DropSumOver -> True,\n  \
FinalSubstitutions -> {FCGV[\"MU\"] -> 0, FCGV[\"MC\"] -> 0}] /. SMP[\"g_s\"] \
-> gs /. GaugeXi[_] -> 1];     (* massless quarks, Feynman gauge \
*)\nreference = <|pa -> pb, pb -> pa, p -> pa, pd -> pa|>;         (* \
reference vectors of the physical polarization sums *)\npolarizationSum[l_, \
mu_, nu_] := With[{r = reference[l]}, -MTD[mu, nu] + (FVD[l, mu] FVD[r, nu] + \
FVD[r, mu] FVD[l, nu])/SPD[l, r]];\ncircular[l_, mu_, nu_] := Contract[I \
LC[mu, nu, al, be] FV[l, al] FV[reference[l], be]/(2 SP[l, reference[l]])];   \
 (* four-dimensional; contracted here so that the dummy indices do not repeat \
*)\n(* spin and colour averages of the incoming partons; a polarized gluon \
(LL) carries its 1/2 in the circular density *)\naverage[ch_, spinCase_] := \
Times @@ (Switch[#, \"g\", If[spinCase === \"LL\", 1, 1/(D - 2)]/(Nc^2 - 1), \
_, 1/(2 Nc)] & /@ ch[[1 ;; 2]]);\ncolourFactors[expr_] := Factor[expr /. SUNN \
-> Nc] /. (-1 + Nc) (1 + Nc) -> 2 Nc CF /. Nc -> CA;\n\n(* density matrices: \
which incoming (and tagged) momenta get gamma5 insertions *)\ntag[l_] := \
Symbol[ToString[l] <> \"Spin\"];\nsquare[ch_, spinCase_] := Module[{amp = \
amplitude[ch], conj, expr, gluons, indices, polarizedQuarks, polarizedGluons, \
taggedQuark},\n  polarizedQuarks = If[spinCase === \"LL\", {pa, \
pb}[[Position[ch[[1 ;; 2]], Except[\"g\"], {1}, Heads -> False][[All, 1]]]], \
{}];\n  polarizedGluons = If[spinCase === \"LL\", {pa, pb}[[Position[ch[[1 ;; \
2]], \"g\", {1}, Heads -> False][[All, 1]]]], {}];\n  gluons = \
Union[Cases[amp, Polarization[l_, __] :> l, Infinity]];\n  indices = \
Association @ Table[gluons[[i]] -> {Symbol[\"mu\" <> ToString[i]], \
Symbol[\"nu\" <> ToString[i]]}, {i, Length[gluons]}];\n  conj = \
ComplexConjugate[amp];\n  expr = amp conj;\n  (* rename the spinors of \
polarized legs so that the slash FermionSpinSum produces can be replaced by \
the density *)\n  expr = expr /. (With[{l = #, lTag = tag[#]}, Spinor[c_. \
Momentum[l, D], m_, o_] :> Spinor[c Momentum[lTag, D], m, o]] & /@ \
polarizedQuarks);\n  expr = expr /. Flatten[Table[{Momentum[Polarization[l, \
I, ___], D] -> LorentzIndex[indices[l][[1]], D],\n    \
Momentum[Polarization[l, -I, ___], D] -> LorentzIndex[indices[l][[2]], D]}, \
{l, gluons}]];\n  expr = expr Times @@ Table[If[MemberQ[polarizedGluons, l], \
circular[l, indices[l][[1]], indices[l][[2]]], polarizationSum[l, \
indices[l][[1]], indices[l][[2]]]], {l, gluons}];\n  expr = \
FermionSpinSum[FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit[expr]];\n  (* p-slash gamma5 for a \
quark, -p-slash gamma5 for an antiquark (v vbar = (1 - lambda gamma5) \
p-slash/2); the 1/2 is in the average *)\n  expr = expr /. (With[{l = #, lTag \
= tag[#], sign = If[StringEndsQ[ch[[Position[{pa, pb}, #][[1, 1]]]], \"b\"], \
-1, 1]},\n    DiracGamma[Momentum[lTag, D], D] :> sign GSD[l].GA[5]] & /@ \
polarizedQuarks);\n  expr = DiracSimplify[expr, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] \
// Contract;\n  expr = SUNSimplify[expr, Explicit -> True, SUNNToCACF -> \
False] // Contract // ExpandScalarProduct;\n  \
colourFactors[Together[average[ch, spinCase] expr/gs^4 /. u -> -s - t]]];", 
   "Input"], Cell["Amplitude records for the FORM and Tracer routes", 
   "Section"], Cell["The same FeynArts amplitudes, written as plain records \
(one coefficient and the open fermion chains per term; vocabulary in \
FeynFacet/Amplitudes.wl), so that 2-Algebra-FORM.wl and 2-Algebra-Tracer.wl \
square exactly the amplitudes squared here, with their own Dirac, Lorentz and \
colour algebra.  The four-gluon vertex carries a FeynCalc dummy colour index \
($AL$nnn, a different number in every session); it is renamed Glu6 (FeynArts \
numbers the external gluon colours Glu1..Glu4 and the propagator Glu5), so \
that the file is reproducible.", "Text"], Cell["fourGluonDummy[x_Symbol] := \
StringStartsQ[SymbolName[x], \"$AL\"];\nrecords = Association @ \
Table[name[ch] -> (AmplitudeRecords[amplitude[ch]] /. x_Symbol /; \
fourGluonDummy[x] :> Glu6), {ch, channels}];\nRequire[FreeQ[records, x_Symbol \
/; StringStartsQ[SymbolName[x], \"$\"]], \"A FeynCalc dummy symbol is left in \
the records\"];\nSaveAmplitudes[<|\"Channels\" -> Map[name, channels], \
\"Records\" -> records|>];\nShowRecords[records[\"q g -> q\"]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["All channels, both spin cases", "Section"], 
  Cell["born = Association @ Table[spinCase -> Association @ Table[name[ch] \
-> square[ch, spinCase], {ch, channels}], {spinCase, {\"UU\", \
\"LL\"}}];\nTableForm[Normal[Map[Simplify[# /. D -> 4] &, born[\"UU\"]]]]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Checks in four dimensions against the textbook table \
(Ellis, Stirling and Webber, QCD and Collider Physics, Table 7.1, at Nc = 3; \
the polarized quark channels follow from helicity conservation, e.g. q qb -> \
qp qpb only through opposite helicities), written with s + t + u = 0.  The \
identical-quark channel q q -> q keeps no factor 1/2 (two ways of tagging), \
so it is twice the table entry.  The Born terms of all ten Born classes, \
including the polarized gluon channels, are also compared with the reference \
codes in Processes/Hadronic.", "Text"], Cell["textbook = <|\n  \"q qp -> q\" \
-> CF/CA (s^2 + u^2)/t^2,\n  \"q qpb -> q\" -> CF/CA (s^2 + u^2)/t^2,\n  \"q \
q -> q\" -> 2 (CF/CA ((s^2 + u^2)/t^2 + (s^2 + t^2)/u^2) - 2 CF/CA^2 s^2/(t \
u))/2,\n  \"q qb -> q\" -> CF/CA ((s^2 + u^2)/t^2 + (u^2 + t^2)/s^2) - 2 \
CF/CA^2 u^2/(s t),\n  \"q qb -> qp\" -> CF/CA (t^2 + u^2)/s^2,\n  \"q qb -> \
g\" -> 2 CF^2/CA (t^2 + u^2)/(t u) - 2 CF (t^2 + u^2)/s^2,\n  \"q g -> q\" -> \
-CF/CA (s^2 + u^2)/(s u) + (s^2 + u^2)/t^2,\n  \"g g -> g\" -> 9/2 (3 - t \
u/s^2 - s u/t^2 - s t/u^2),\n  \"g g -> q\" -> 1/(2 CA) (t^2 + u^2)/(t u) - \
CA/(CA^2 - 1) (t^2 + u^2)/s^2|>;\ntextbookLL = <|\n  \"q qp -> q\" -> CF/CA \
(s^2 - u^2)/t^2,\n  \"q qb -> qp\" -> -CF/CA (t^2 + u^2)/s^2,\n  \"q g -> q\" \
-> -CF/CA (s^2 - u^2)/(s u) + (s^2 - u^2)/t^2,\n  \"g g -> q\" -> -(1/(2 CA) \
(t^2 + u^2)/(t u) - CA/(CA^2 - 1) (t^2 + u^2)/s^2)|>;\ncheck[spinCase_, \
table_] := Association @ KeyValueMap[\n  #1 -> Simplify[(born[spinCase][#1] \
/. D -> 4) - #2 /. u -> -s - t /. {CF -> 4/3, CA -> 3}] &, \
table];\nRequire[And @@ (# === 0 & /@ Values[check[\"UU\", textbook]]) && And \
@@ (# === 0 & /@ Values[check[\"LL\", textbookLL]]),\n  \"A Born square \
differs from the textbook table\", {check[\"UU\", textbook], check[\"LL\", \
textbookLL]}];\n{check[\"UU\", textbook], check[\"LL\", textbookLL]}", 
   "Input"], Cell["Crossing: the incoming-leg permutation b a -> c equals a b \
-> c with t <-> u; the LL difference is symmetric under the exchange as \
well.", "Text"], Cell["swap[expr_] := expr /. t -> -s - t;         (* t <-> u \
with u = -s-t *)\ncrossingPairs = {{\"q qp -> q\", \"qp q -> q\"}, {\"q g -> \
q\", \"g q -> q\"}, {\"q g -> g\", \"g q -> g\"}, {\"q qb -> q\", \"qb q -> \
q\"}};\nRequire[And @@ Flatten[Table[Simplify[born[sc][pair[[2]]] - \
swap[born[sc][pair[[1]]]]] === 0, {sc, {\"UU\", \"LL\"}}, {pair, \
crossingPairs}]],\n  \"Crossing relation between incoming-leg permutations \
fails\"];\n\"crossing relations hold\"", "Input"], Cell["Save", "Section"], 
  Cell["result = <|\"Born\" -> born, \"Channels\" -> Map[name, channels], \
\"Variables\" -> \"s, t (u = -s-t), D, CF, CA; divided by \
gs^4\"|>;\nSaveResult[\"Born\", result];\nKeys[born[\"UU\"]]", "Input"]}, 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
